x87 at PC=24 kept as binary32: an operation is one host instruction.

Patch 06 keeps the x87 stack as host doubles across a translation block,
and at PC=24 (what Direct3D sets, so every 3D game's whole frame) it
rounded every result to 24 bits through two conversions -- binary64 to
binary32 and back, then an xor for the inexact flag -- on the dependent
chain, after the operation and its window check. In 3DMark 99's
first-person test the x87 forms were 24 % of the frame at 2.9 profile
samples per instruction against 1.2 for an integer register form (the
form weights of tools/tcg-form-weights.py, 2026-09-11).

At PC=24 the shadows are now binary32, in i32 globals of their own
(cpu_x87_ss[], env->x87_ss[]), and with the inexact flag already sticky
(TB_FLAG_X87_PE, patch 37 -- the state a game's loop runs in) an
operation is the host's own binary32 instruction plus one range check:
+, -, *, / and sqrt correctly rounded to 24 bits is exactly what the x87
computes at PC=24 while the result has a binary32 exponent. A result
that would not have one takes the slow path -- overflow, underflow, and
the lowest binade, which is excluded on purpose: a value just below
2^-126 rounds up to 2^-126 in binary32 (fewer bits there) but not at 24
significant bits with the x87's 15-bit exponent, and only that binade
can tell the two roundings apart. Operands may sit in it (exact); results
may not. While PE is still to be decided the operands are widened and the
binary64 path runs as before, its residuals feeding PE and its rounding
to 24 bits being the result (exact for the same reason as before:
53 >= 2 * 24 + 2). fld m32 is the operand's own bits after the zero-or-
normal check, fst m32 the shadow's own bits with no check and no flag,
m64 loads round through one conversion, fist/frndint/fst m64 widen (one
conversion) and keep their binary64 code, fild narrows its exact binary64
integer. A reload from fpregs[] accepts exponents -126..127 (the top
binade was outside the old window), the unwinder (tcg-cpu.c) converts
from binary32 for a block translated in mode 2.

Exact: tools/x87-guest-test.py identical with x87-fast on and off,
709,893 result lines, now including a second sweep of every control word
with PE set before each case -- without it (fninit before every case) the
battery never ran the sticky variant at all, patch 37's included.

